# The KDOS defaults for GSettings, which is where a GTK application on the host
# reads its theme: directly, or through the Settings portal, whose
# org.gnome.desktop.* keys xdg-desktop-portal-gtk serves from these same
# GSettings. GTK on Wayland takes org.gnome.desktop.interface from one of the
# two over ~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini, and once gsettings-desktop-schemas
# is installed an unset key there is the schema's default — Adwaita,
# Cantarell. GTK 4 always reads the portal; GTK 3 reads it under
# GTK_USE_PORTAL=1, which every login exports, and directly otherwise. Neither
# route carries gtk-modules: GTK 3 takes those from kde-gtk-config's
# org.gtk.Settings, and the gtk3 port is patched to open it beside the portal.
#
# These are DEFAULTS, not settings: a value a person sets with `gsettings set`
# lives in their dconf database and wins over this file. In a Plasma session
# kde-gtk-config's kded module writes every one of these keys into that
# database from the KDE settings, so this file answers only before the first
# session, and for a GTK program started outside one.
#
# An override takes effect only once glib-compile-schemas has read it into
# gschemas.compiled. kpkg's schemas trigger rebuilds that index whenever an
# installed package touches this directory, and 70_image/050_theme.sh
# rebuilds it once more, so a change here reaches an image without a schema
# package being reinstalled.
#
# Every value is what kde-gtk-config writes for the default look, bone: the
# Breeze GTK theme, which colours itself from the KDE scheme, the KDOS icons,
# Breeze's cursor, and the two faces kdeglobals names, which fontconfig also
# puts first for `sans-serif` and `monospace`. Bone is dark, so the colour
# scheme preference is dark. Font rendering needs no line: the schema's own
# defaults, greyscale antialiasing with slight hinting, are the rendering
# kdeglobals names.
#
# This override is the only GTK default KDOS ships. GTK reads every
# gtk-3.0/settings.ini and gtk-4.0/settings.ini along /etc and
# XDG_CONFIG_DIRS in list order with the LAST one winning, so a settings.ini
# in /usr/share/kdos/xdg would outrank the administrator's in /etc; and on
# Wayland GTK takes these keys from GSettings, which this file seeds, before
# any settings.ini.

[org.gnome.desktop.interface]
gtk-theme='Breeze'
icon-theme='KDOS'
cursor-theme='breeze_cursors'
cursor-size=24
color-scheme='prefer-dark'
font-name='Noto Sans 10'
document-font-name='Noto Sans 10'
monospace-font-name='JetBrains Mono 10'
